## 5. What the live site does not have

Checked across the home page and all seven probed routes. Nothing invented to
fill these; sections requiring invention were not built.

| Missing | Handling |
|---|---|
| **Named projects / case studies** | The live "Portfolio" holds product photography only — no names, clients, sites or dates. Rebuilt honestly as **Equipment** with hardware captions. Brief Section 5 flag raised: **there are no project photos on the live site** |
| **Team bios / photos** | None published — no team section built |
| **Testimonials** | None published — none built |
| **Certifications / awards** | None published on-site. Credentials section carries only the **VERIFIED** Bosch listing, the **EXTRACTED** 2018 founding year, and **VERIFIED** GST/Pvt-Ltd status |
| **Statistics** (installs, clients, headcount) | None published — none invented, none shown |
| **Company history** | Only "Established in the year 2018 at Bengaluru, Karnataka". Used exactly that |
| **Social links** | Live footer icons link to `#` (dead) — omitted rather than fabricated |
| **Privacy policy** | Linked to `#`, no page exists — omitted |
| **Form backend** | The live form posts nowhere. Rebuilt to compose a `mailto:` to both real addresses — no fake success state |
| **Video** | None on the live site |

---

## 6. Open blockers

**None blocking the build.** No bracketed placeholders were required — every
contact detail, claim and image resolved to a real extracted or verified source.

For a human decision before go-live:

1. **`logo.png` is a weak source asset** — 3000×2000 with compression artefacts
   baked into the transparent PNG and a soft bevelled treatment. A vector redraw
   would materially lift the design. Not actioned: redrawing a logo is a brand
   decision.
2. **Low-resolution partner logos** — `ss.jpeg` is 200×112 and `ebss.png` is
   112×60; both soften in the marquee. Higher-res versions would help.
3. **Social profiles** — supply real URLs and the footer can carry them.
4. **Privacy policy** — linked but non-existent on the live site.
5. **Form backend** — currently `mailto:`. A real endpoint (Formspree, Resend, or
   a route handler) is a one-file change.
6. **Micro Power alt-text error** on the live site is worth fixing at source.
7. **No project photography exists.** If CPK has site/installation photos, an
   actual projects section becomes possible — currently it cannot be built
   honestly.

---

## 7. Build

- Next.js 15.1.6 App Router · TypeScript (strict) · Tailwind CSS 3.4
- **Lenis** — global smooth scroll, driven off the GSAP ticker so ScrollTrigger
  and Lenis share one clock; anchor links routed through `lenis.scrollTo`
- **GSAP + ScrollTrigger** — scrubbed parallax on the hero photograph and the
  About product frame
- **Framer Motion** — word-by-word hero headline reveal, `whileInView` fade-ups,
  staggered rails, hover zoom inside `overflow-hidden`, mobile menu transitions
- **Marquee** — pure CSS keyframe, no package
- `lucide-react` for system icons; all brand marks are real assets
- `prefers-reduced-motion` respected throughout (Lenis skipped, parallax skipped)
- No dark sections

`npm run build` → clean, zero errors.

### Verified in a real browser (Playwright)

| Check | desktop 1440 | tablet 834 | mobile 390 |
|---|---|---|---|
| Images rendered / broken | 36 / **0** | 36 / **0** | 36 / **0** |
| Horizontal overflow | none | none | none |
| Empty containers | none | none | none |
| Console errors | none | none | none |
| HTTP ≥400 responses | none | none | none |
| `<h1>` count | 1 | 1 | 1 |

Hover-reveals, marquee, parallax, scroll reveals and the mobile menu were all
exercised against the running server.

> Note for future runs: do not run `npm run build` while `next dev` is live —
> they share `.next` and the dev server will serve a corrupted bundle.
